  "content": {
    "id": "v2-47999-p62-practice-slot-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Factorise by equating coefficients, given $3x^3-5x^2-4x+4=(x-2)(ax^2+bx+c)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3$, $b=1$, $c=-2$; $(x-2)(x+1)(3x-2)$.",
      "worked": "Expand the supplied factorisation:\n$$(x-2)(ax^2+bx+c)=ax^3+(b-2a)x^2+(c-2b)x-2c.$$\nEquating coefficients gives\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=3\\\\b-2a&=-5\\\\c-2b&=-4\\\\-2c&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=3$, $b=1$ and $c=-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^3-5x^2-4x+4&=(x-2)(3x^2+x-2)\\\\&=(x-2)(3x^2+3x-2x-2)\\\\&=(x-2)(3x(x+1)-2(x+1))\\\\&=(x-2)(x+1)(3x-2).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
